# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Nothing in this block is ever committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env` holds the real OPENAI_API_KEY, BRAVE_API_KEY, EXA_API_KEY and
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY. `.env.example` is the committed template and is the one
# deliberate exception — keep it free of live values.
#
# The `.env.*` glob is what catches the variants that get created by hand
# later (.env.production, .env.staging, web/.env.local). Listing only `.env`
# is how a key eventually ships: someone copies it to a new suffix and the
# old rule does not reach.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
# The Playwright template too. It carries variable NAMES and a note on what
# kind of Clerk account to use — no values. The file it describes,
# web/.env.test, stays ignored.
!web/.env.test.example

# Anything a credential tends to land in.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets.json
service-account*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# Playwright. .env.test holds a real Clerk account, and e2e/.auth holds a live
# signed-in session — either one in a commit is a credential leak.
web/.env.test
web/e2e/.auth/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mock data is re-seeded from mocks/seeds/ on first run, or via /api/reset.
# The seeds are committed; the working copy under mocks/data/ is not.
mocks/data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Single-line ~344KB export from the design tool, with fonts and images
# inlined as base64. The real UI is web/src; this is a reference snapshot and
# would sit in the history forever.
Northbound Prototype.html

DEMO_SCRIPT*
slide*

.DS_Store
*.swp
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/
